+                /* An attempt that wrote data to the sink resumes where it
+                   stopped, so it does not use up the retry budget: a large
+                   download whose connection keeps breaking (for example
+                   an HTTP/2 stream reset while the transfer was paused
+                   because the sink was slow) must not fail after
+                   `download-attempts` tries that each moved it forward.
+                   Only tries in a row without progress count. A server
+                   can still keep a download going by sending a little
+                   before each break, but it can already do that within a
+                   single try (`stalled-download-timeout`), so this adds
+                   no new way to hang. */
